<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bundelas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundelas</a> are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> clan of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> who gave their name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>. Rising in the 16th century under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudra-pratap-singh">Rudra Pratap Singh</a>, who founded Orchha in 1531, they built kingdoms that alternately served and resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrasal">Chhatrasal</a> of Panna won independence for much of the region in the late 17th century. Their many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> survived under British paramountcy until after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a>.</p></div>
